  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Thursday)\nIssued at 1255 PM MST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nLatest satellite imagery around midday shows the approaching\ntrough that will give NE WY and W SD the next round of light \nprecip and cooler weather. At the surface, the winds have swung to\nthe west-to-northwest for the western half of the CWA, indicating\nthat the cold front is pushing through. Wind speeds have been \nslowing increasing late this morning.\n\nFor Friday afternoon into Friday evening, precip streaming up from\nthe SW will collide with the cold air from the NW. So for those in\nNE WY and in far W SD, precip will likely start as rain. But as\ntemps cool down, the rain will switch to snow from NW to SE.\n\nFor tonight into Saturday, a colder air mass will finish it's move\nthrough the CWA. This means that any lingering light rain showers\nwill switch to light snow showers tonight with mainly light snow\nexpected Saturday. That being said, slightly warmer temps in parts\nof SW SD and the W SD plains could mean a snow/rain mix in the\nafternoon before it switches back to all snow late Saturday.\nPrecip will diminish from NW to SE Saturday night. Overnight lows\ntonight will be in the 20s to low 30s, Saturday afternoon highs\nwill be in the 30s to near 40.\n\nAs far as snowfall amounts go, the greatest expected snowfall is\nin NE WY and the Black Hills where forecasted amounts are around \n1 to 3 inches late this afternoon through Saturday. That being\nsaid, there is a 10-30% chance of 4 inches, or more, of snow. So\nlow probability but very isolated spots in the Black Hills could \nsee more than 3 inches. And solar heating may limit the totals, \nas well as any impacts.\n\nFor Sunday and Monday, the colder weather remains in place with\nexpected highs in the 30s, lows in the teens to near 20. A quick\nmoving upper level trough could bring some light snow to the Black\nHills so there is a slight chance for light snow late Monday into\nMonday night.\n\nTuesday through the rest of next week, mainly dry weather is\nlikely with slowly warming afternoon highs. Morning temps look to\nstay on the cooler side, mostly in the 20s, but afternoon highs\nwill be in the 40s to 50s. Temps like this are near to slightly \nabove normal for late November.",
